  "text": "Accessibility Tools\nSkip to main content\nGive Dr. Paul O'Malley a phone call at\n(747) 364-0020\nFree Holistic Dental Course\nHome\nAbout Us\nServices\nGallery\nVideos\nAreas We Serve\nResources\nBlog\nContact Us\nHome\nServices\nUltra Thin Veneers\nUltra-Thin Veneers\nin Los Angeles\n\nAchieve a flawless smile: Experience the elegance and durability of ultra thin veneers in Los Angeles and Encino.\n\nTransform Your Smile\nwith Ultra-Thin Veneers\n\nNatural-Looking Results with Minimal Tooth Alteration. At Dr. Paul O'Malley's practice, we specialize in ultra-thin veneers that offer a minimally invasive solution for achieving a beautiful, natural-looking smile. Our approach focuses on providing aesthetic enhancements while ensuring the health and integrity of your natural teeth. These veneers are meticulously crafted from high-quality materials that closely mimic the appearance and texture of natural enamel. By utilizing advanced techniques, we ensure that the application process involves minimal alteration to your existing tooth structure. This method not only enhances the aesthetic appeal of your smile but also maintains the strength and health of your teeth, providing you with a durable and long-lasting solution.\n\nKelley & Jeff's Journey with Dr. O'Malley\nWhat Are Ultra-Thin Veneers?\n\nMinimally Invasive Cosmetic Restorations for a Natural and Durable Smile.\n\nUltra-thin veneers are a type of cosmetic dental restoration made from high-quality, durable materials that expertly mimic the translucency and texture of natural enamel. These advanced veneers offer a revolutionary solution compared to traditional veneers, which often necessitate significant removal of tooth enamel. Designed to be as thin as a contact lens, ultra-thin veneers require minimal tooth alteration, thereby preserving more of your natural tooth structure. This innovative approach not only maintains the health and integrity of your teeth but also ensures a stronger and longer-lasting result. By choosing ultra-thin veneers in Los Angeles with Dr. Paul O'Malley, you benefit from a minimally invasive treatment that enhances your smile while supporting your overall oral health.\n\nCase 1: Not All Veneers are the Same\n\n4\n\nAppointments\n\n2\n\nMonths Time\n\n93%\n\nPercent Change\n\n69k\n\nTotal Investment\nBefore & After\n\nI really enjoyed working on this case. We decided to choose a brighter shade to complement her olive skin. The character of her teeth needed to reflect her fun, caring, and outgoing personality. I'm thrilled with how natural the veneers look—as if she's never had any work done. I suggested she simply tell people she took good care of her teeth and had braces as a child. She does, and people believe her. The subtle nuances in the shape and size of the veneers make a significant difference. She was also tired of constantly needing fillings for her back teeth, and it was time to put an end to that cycle. She looks stunning.\n\n* time required and number of total appointments are variable based on your specific needs and circumstances. In other words sometimes we can complete cases in two weeks, for others it may be longer.\n\nReveal amount of after image\nBefore uppers – needs mercury removal\nBefore lowers – large leaking fillings\nPreplanning!\nTemps – checking final color\nAfter uppers\nAfter lowers\nFinal veneers retracted\nWow!\nAfter Smile\nBiomimetic Dentistry for a Healthier, More Radiant You\nFeel confident in your smile again\nAccess the Free Course\nAbout Us\nServices\nGallery\nVideos\nAreas We Serve\nResources\nBlog\n\nLocation\n\n16661 Ventura Blvd. Ste. 800\nEncino, CA 91436\n\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nContact\n\nCall Dr. Paul O'Malley on the phone at\n(747) 364-0020\n\nHours Of Operation\n\nMon-Wed  |  10am-6pm\nThurs-Fri  |  By Appointment\nSat-Sun  |  Closed\n\nDR. PAUL O'MALLEY REVIEWS:\n\n4.8 Stars 86 Reviews\n\n    \n\n(OPENS IN A NEW TAB)\n\nStay Connected\n\n© Dr. Paul O'Malley. All Rights Reserved.\n\nTerms & Conditions Privacy Policy Sitemap\n\nDigital Marketing & Design\nby Studio 3 Marketing®\n(opens in a new tab)\nAccessibility: If you are vision-impaired or have some other impairment covered by the Americans with Disabilities Act or a similar law, and you wish to discuss potential accommodations related to using this website, please contact our Accessibility Manager at (818) 616-8838.\nContact Us"
